        "text": "3. 8. 22.",
        "@annotation": {
         "@id": "copies/xj540rr2929#transcription-annotation",
         "belief": {
          "@type": "belief",
          "@id": "copies/xj540rr2929#transcription-belief",
          "certainty": "likely",
          "reasons": [
           {
            "@type": "meaningComprehension",
            "comprehends": [
             "copies/xj540rr2929#inscription"
            ],
            "note": "Graded medium on the figures of the date: one figure is arguable. Fine pencil, four figures with points between them and nothing else in the crop. Day and month are plain, the 8 showing both loops closed. The two year figures are the same glyph twice, a small top loop over a stroke that falls to the left and curls back at the foot, which I read as the cursive 2 of these hands; read as 9 it would give 1929, outside the range of the corpus. Crops 1 and 2 hold only creases and perforations."
           }
          ]
         }
        }
       }
      }
     ]
    }
   ],
   "scan": "https://stacks.stanford.edu/image/iiif/xj540rr2929%2Fxj540rr2929_0001/",
